# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Configuration template.
#  The interactive console configures its model provider through
#  `dfir-agent setup` and stores credentials in a separate local config
#  directory. This template documents the optional environment variables the
#  runtime also understands. Copy it to `.env` and fill in the values you need.
#  `.env` is ignored by Git and must never be committed.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# === Model provider credential (OpenRouter) =================================
# Used when a credential is supplied through the environment rather than the
# console setup flow. Leave blank and use `dfir-agent setup` for normal use.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1

# === Question scope triage (optional) =======================================
# Before an investigation is opened the console asks the SAME configured model,
# in one small request, whether the input concerns the loaded case, and refuses
# it when the answer is OFFTOPIC. On by default. Set this to 0 to take the
# triage out entirely: no request is made, nothing is refused before the run,
# and every question reaches the investigation. That is the setting a model
# comparison wants -- the triage spends a request of the model under test, and
# a weaker model refuses legitimate follow-up questions, so the measurement
# scores the triage instead of the investigation. Each run records which of the
# two configurations it ran under, in the case_open entry of its oversight log.
# DFA_SCOPE_TRIAGE=1

# === External forensic program paths (optional) ==============================
# Set these explicitly when a program is not on PATH. Otherwise the runtime
# searches PATH and the usual installation directories.
# DFA_VOL=
# DFA_TSHARK=
# DFA_TESSERACT=
# DFA_CLAMSCAN=

# === Where content extracted from the evidence is written ===================
# Anything a tool reconstructs out of the evidence -- carved files, archive
# members a scanner unpacked, dumped memory regions -- is a real payload of
# whatever that evidence carries. This directory is where all of it goes, and it
# must be storage the host filesystem cannot see: a Docker named volume or a
# tmpfs, never a bind mount. The containerized console sets it to the named
# volume declared in its Compose definition. Where it is unset or points at a
# bind-mounted directory, the tools that reconstruct file content refuse to run
# rather than write a payload where the host can reach it -- and where an
# on-access antivirus scanner can delete one out from under the tool that is
# still writing it, which truncates that tool's output without saying so.
# DFA_PAYLOAD_ROOT=

# === Containerized signature scanning (optional) ============================
# When configured, memory_malware_scan runs entirely inside this image. Extracted
# memory regions may contain real malicious payloads, so they remain on a noexec
# tmpfs in the container and never touch the host filesystem. That holds for THIS
# ROUTE only: without this setting the scan runs locally and writes the same
# extracted regions below DFA_VOL_WORKDIR, which is contained only when
# DFA_PAYLOAD_ROOT is. Without this setting the scanner also requires a local
# clamscan installation.
# DFA_MEMORY_SCAN_DOCKER_IMAGE=
# Prebuilt Volatility symbol cache. Cold indexing may exceed the runtime budget.
# DFA_VOL_CACHE_SEED=
# One local symbol directory mounted read-only into the container. A list of
# multiple host directories is not forwarded because it cannot be mapped
# faithfully to one container path.
# DFA_VOL_SYMBOL_DIRS=
